From: phpguard <local>
Subject: [PATCH] ext/standard: Hold serialize_lock over userland Serializable::unserialize() dispatch

User code run by a Serializable::unserialize() handler can call
unserialize()/serialize() recursively while the outer stream is still
mid-parse and share its var_hash (php_var_unserialize_init reuses the
outer context when BG(serialize_lock) == 0 and level > 0). The nested
parse mutates/frees entries the outer parse still references ->
use-after-free on freed property slots (PHP UAF class, Oct 2026
embargo, CVE-2026-109618/109619 candidates).

Lock the dispatch for userland classes only: internal handlers (SPL
coding wrappers) re-enter php_var_unserialize() intentionally and
depend on the shared var_hash for outer R:/r: back-reference
numbering - locking them shifts slot indices and breaks 11 core
phpt tests (see research/gate-regression-triage.md).

---

diff --git a/ext/standard/var_unserializer.re b/ext/standard/var_unserializer.re
index 353c7086..0c70474d 100644
--- a/ext/standard/var_unserializer.re
+++ b/ext/standard/var_unserializer.re
@@ -773,8 +773,25 @@ static inline int object_custom(UNSERIALIZE_PARAMETER, zend_class_entry *ce)
 	if (ce->unserialize == NULL) {
 		zend_error(E_WARNING, "Class %s has no unserializer", ZSTR_VAL(ce->name));
 		object_init_ex(rval, ce);
-	} else if (ce->unserialize(rval, ce, (const unsigned char*)*p, datalen, (zend_unserialize_data *)var_hash) != SUCCESS) {
-		return 0;
+	} else {
+		/* Serializable::unserialize() runs user code that may call
+		 * unserialize() recursively: hold serialize_lock over the dispatch
+		 * so a nested call gets its own var_hash instead of sharing ours
+		 * (freed-property-slot UAF, Oct 2026 CVE class). Internal handlers
+		 * (SPL coding wrappers etc.) share the var_hash by design, so they
+		 * must stay unlocked. */
+		if (ce->type & ZEND_INTERNAL_CLASS) {
+			if (ce->unserialize(rval, ce, (const unsigned char*)*p, datalen, (zend_unserialize_data *)var_hash) != SUCCESS) {
+				return 0;
+			}
+		} else {
+			BG(serialize_lock)++;
+			zend_result tmp = ce->unserialize(rval, ce, (const unsigned char*)*p, datalen, (zend_unserialize_data *)var_hash);
+			BG(serialize_lock)--;
+			if (tmp != SUCCESS) {
+				return 0;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	(*p) += datalen + 1; /* +1 for '}' */
